  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "\"Can\" is a versatile modal verb used to express ability (\"I can swim\"), permission (\"Can I go?\"), possibility (\"It can rain\"), or to make requests/offers (\"Can you help?\"). Synonyms include be able to, know how to, be allowed to, and may. It functions in the present tense, with \"could\" as its past tense counterpart. Usage Examples of \"Can\" (Modal Verb): Ability/Skill: \"She can speak three languages\". Permission: \"Can I use your phone?\". Possibility: \"It can get very cold here in winter\". Request/Offer: \"Can you pass the salt?\" or \"I can help you with that\". Synonyms and Related Phrases: Ability: Be able to, have the capacity to, know how to. Permission: May, be allowed to, have the right to, authorized to. Possibility: Could, might, potentially. Noun Usage:\"Can\" also refers to a metal container (e.g., \"a soda can\") or the act of preserving food (\"to can tomatoes\").",
